WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.780
What are P and NP,

2
00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.880
and what does verification mean?

3
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.020
We will separate finding a

4
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.700
solution from checking a complete

5
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.940
certificate, explain why P is

6
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.160
contained in NP, and examine

7
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.760
a tempting but invalid universal-tour

8
00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:15.080
claim.

9
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.340
P contains decision problems solvable

10
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.620
by a deterministic algorithm in

11
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.600
polynomial worst-case time. A polynomial

12
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.900
bound is an asymptotic classification,

13
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.440
not a promise that every

14
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.400
polynomial algorithm is practical for

15
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.300
every input size.

16
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.280
NP contains decision problems whose

17
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:37.600
yes-instances have polynomial-length certificates that

18
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.460
a deterministic polynomial-time procedure can

19
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.680
verify. The course's equivalent description

20
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:45.540
uses a nondeterministic guess followed

21
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.080
by verification, not ordinary random

22
00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.920
guessing with a guaranteed good

23
00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:50.360
outcome.

24
00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.080
For a TSP threshold question,

25
00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:54.820
a certificate can list a

26
00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:57.160
proposed tour. The verifier must

27
00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:58.900
check the vertices, all required

28
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.000
edges, the closing return and

29
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.700
the total cost, rather than

30
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.400
accepting because the route merely

31
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.340
looks plausible.

32
00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.440
A route that repeats a

33
00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.640
vertex and omits another fails

34
00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:10.680
even if it is cheap.

35
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.780
A route visiting every vertex

36
00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.280
also fails if its cost

37
00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.600
exceeds K, because the certificate

38
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.000
must establish the entire yes-condition.

39
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.840
For knapsack, a certificate can

40
00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.120
specify the selected item indices.

41
00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.160
Check that no item is

42
00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.260
repeated, total weight is at

43
00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.300
most capacity and total profit

44
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.980
is at least the requested

45
00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:34.840
threshold, with numeric operations accounted

46
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.660
for in the representation model.

47
00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:39.660
If one candidate fails verification,

48
00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.720
only that candidate has been

49
00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:44.460
rejected. Another candidate may succeed,

50
00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:46.440
so failure of a proposed

51
00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.460
certificate does not establish that

52
00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:49.660
the whole input is a

53
00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:50.400
no-instance.

54
00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:52.860
Every problem in P also

55
00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.780
belongs to NP, because a

56
00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.840
polynomial verifier can simply run

57
00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.560
the polynomial solver. It does

58
00:01:58.560 --> 00:01:59.980
not need a useful certificate

59
00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:02.400
at all, which immediately disproves

60
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.860
the idea that NP means

61
00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:04.760
not polynomial.

62
00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.780
The absence of a known

63
00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:08.580
efficient algorithm is not part

64
00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.320
of the NP membership definition.

65
00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.000
Whether P equals NP is

66
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.600
unresolved in the course framework,

67
00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.080
so do not draw a

68
00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.000
strict separation as an established

69
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:18.400
theorem.

70
00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:20.980
Compare the question whether some

71
00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:22.440
tour costs at most K

72
00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.480
with the question whether every

73
00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.280
tour does. A single cheap

74
00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.720
tour witnesses the existential yes-condition,

75
00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.880
but cannot establish that every

76
00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:31.960
other tour is cheap.

77
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.940
For the universal question, one

78
00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.040
expensive tour can instead witness

79
00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.240
a no-answer. This complementary-certificate observation

80
00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:42.580
does not prove that the

81
00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:45.040
universal problem lies outside NP

82
00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.340
or requires exponential time, despite

83
00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.820
the unsupported claims on the

84
00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:50.220
slide.

85
00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.880
Certificate length must be polynomial

86
00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.860
as well as verification time,

87
00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:56.600
and the verifier checks a

88
00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.640
yes-witness for the exact decision

89
00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.840
predicate. Guessing a whole enormous

90
00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.940
computation is not useful if

91
00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.920
merely reading the claimed certificate

92
00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.860
already exceeds the allowed bound.

93
00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.840
Things to take note of:

94
00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:11.580
define the decision question, give

95
00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.200
a complete witness and explain

96
00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:16.020
every verification check. Keep solving

97
00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:18.340
separate from checking, remember P

98
00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.360
is inside NP, and never

99
00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:21.680
turn a failed witness into

100
00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.580
a proof of nonexistence, how

101
00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:24.100
charming.
